<title>GREECE: Greece to cut T-bill rates by 60 bps May 14.</title>
<headline>Greece to cut T-bill rates by 60 bps May 14.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's finance ministry said it will slash its three-, six-, 12-month T-bill rates by 60 basis points to 8.6 percent, 8.9 percent and 9.7 percent respectively effective May 14.</p>
<p>It is the first time ever that the benchmark 12-month T-bill features a single-digit interest rate. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
